      "sourceTextSha256": "727c46c944faadace220c46933b57088fc0e08e2f88bb753eca5ffb8b8e49ddf",
      "text": "Days 2–3 take you through the Drake Passage, with salt winds, ocean swells and seabirds accompanying the voyage south. You may spot a fin whale. Look out for wandering, grey-headed and black-browed albatrosses, light-mantled albatrosses, Cape petrels, southern fulmars, Wilson’s storm petrels, blue petrels and Antarctic petrels.",
